<title>USA: Centex Corp Q4 shr $0.98 vs $0.54.</title>
<headline>Centex Corp Q4 shr $0.98 vs $0.54.</headline>
<dateline>DALLAS 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>CENTEX CORPORATION AND SUBSIDIARIES</p>
<p>	   (dollar amounts in thousands, except per share data)</p>
<p>						     Quarter Ended</p>
<p>							March 31</p>
<p>					     1997	    1996  Change</p>
<p> Revenues			    $ 951,870	$ 825,042   15%</p>
<p> Earnings Before Income Taxes     44,579	   25,792   73%</p>
<p> Net Earnings			   29,041	   15,785   84%</p>
<p> Earnings Per Share		     0.98	     0.54   81%</p>
<p> Average Shares Outstanding   29,766,475     29,212,198    2%</p>
<p>						     Year Ended</p>
<p>							March 31</p>
<p>					    1997	     1996  Change</p>
<p> Revenues			    3,784,991	3,102,987   22%</p>
<p> Earnings Before Income Taxes    163,743	   87,786   87%</p>
<p> Net Earnings			  106,563	   53,365  100%</p>
<p> Earnings Per Share		     3.62	     1.83   98%</p>
<p> Average Shares Outstanding   29,429,451     29,090,919    1%</p>
<p>NOTE: Centex owns a 51.4 percent stake in Centex Construction Products Inc.</p>
<p>Beginning with the quarter ended June 30, 1996, CXP's financial results are consolidated with those of Centex and are reflected in Centex's revenues and operating earnings.  In order to facilitate comparisons between years, CXP's operating earnings and the related minority interest in CXP have been reclassified to reflect the total amounts for the quarter ended March 31, 1996.  Had CXP's revenues been consolidated for the quarter ended March 31, 1996, Centex's consolidated revenues for that quarter would have increased by $45,578 to $870,620.</p>
